{
  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best-performing config so far is config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, PCA n2000, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) at 0.619 acc / 0.610 F1. RNA carries most of the signal (RNA-only multiprofile avgpool = 0.591 vs image-only = 0.208), and avgpool aggregation clearly beats transformer (0.591 vs 0.519). However, PCA n2000 is the only RNA encoder tested across all experiments. Question: config_030 swaps only the RNA encoder to SCVI n200 (a learned 200-dim latent) while holding every other hyperparameter identical to config_018. This isolates whether a nonlinear, dimensionality-reduced learned representation can match or beat a 2000-dim linear PCA projection. Why this is the best next experiment: The RNA encoder is the highest-leverage untested design axis because RNA dominates the signal. If SCVI n200 outperforms PCA n2000, it opens a productive direction across all fusion/image-encoder variants; if it underperforms, we confirm PCA's robustness and can redirect budget toward image encoder or fusion strategy. This single experiment reduces the most critical uncertainty with minimal confounds (one-variable change from the current best)."
}

